of the harbour.

The school play was a great success. The children had clearly practised for w=
eeks, and the costumes were remarkable considering most of them were made fro=
m old curtains.

The local library has started a repair cafe once a month. I took the old lamp=
 along, and a retired electrician had it working again within twenty minutes.

The photos from the wedding came out beautifully. I will put a few in the pos=
t for you, as I know you prefer prints to looking at them on a screen.

The hedge finally got its trim on Saturday. It took most of the morning, and =
the garden waste bin is full, but the front of the house looks much tidier fo=
r it.

We watched the meteor shower from the back garden last night. It was cold, bu=
t we saw several bright ones, and the children talked about it all through br=
eakfast.

My knee is much better now, thank you for asking. The physio exercises are du=
ll but they work, and I managed the whole hill on our walk last week without =
stopping.

The fox has been visiting the garden again. We see it most evenings just afte=
r dark, trotting along the fence and stopping to look at the house before it =
goes.

I bumped into your cousin at the station last week. She looked well and asked=
 to be remembered to you; she is still working at the library and seems to en=
joy it.

It was lovely to catch up at the weekend. The garden looked wonderful, and I =
have been meaning to ask what you planted along the fence; the colours were r=
eally striking.

Love to everyone.

